      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 1051: 🔴 This advertises generic NACK, but the media stack has no implementation for it: `MediaDescription` only records `rtcp_fb_nack_pli`, while `SocketPair::readCallback` handles PLI/FIR, REMB, and transport-cc but treats RTPFB FMT\u003d1 (generic NACK) as an unknown RTCP packet, with no retransmission path. A peer can therefore send NACKs believing they were negotiated while Jami ignores them. Implement and wire generic-NACK handling, or do not advertise this capability.",
      "revId": "75881acfa12b1dd08e9b3bb0a6a8714466c3ca23",
